From bc50a352b248ba9b01f431838f582e4f70cda295 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 13:01:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] glyco: correct precursors to the monoisotopic peak from the
 MS1 envelope (#64)

On pGlyco2 mouse liver T-1 the firmware records a class of wide, high-mass
glycopeptide envelopes on an M+3..M+6 isotopologue (88 of 3,824 mass-resolvable
reference scans at exactly +4). Widening --isotope-error reaches them but is
mass-degenerate with a glycan composition change, so arms C/D of #64 piled
hundreds of arbitrary compositions onto the largest allowed offset.

`--precursor-mono auto` (glyco, mzML/.raw) reads the preceding MS1 and fits the
observed envelope at the reported charge against an exact multi-element
glycopeptide isotope model under "the recorded precursor is M+k", k = 0..6
(cosine over M-1..M+n with a zero-weight pre-mono slot). When a k > 0 clears a
fit floor, beats the recorded hypothesis by a margin and its monoisotope is
above the MS1 noise, the precursor is moved down by k-1 isotopes and searched
with the DEFAULT 0..2 window; the sweep's +1 takes the last step so an overshoot
cannot lose the true mass. Never widens. `off` (default) and inputs without MS1
are byte-identical (goldens unchanged; `main` vs this binary flag-off: identical).

Glyco PIN gains MonoShift/MonoFit/MonoFitGain/MonoSNR only when the flag fitted
something; `--precursor-mono-dump` writes every hypothesis' fit per MS2.

Also: `--glyco-index-sequon-only` (hidden) enumerates only N-X-S/T-bearing
peptides into the candidate index (3.4 GB instead of ~27 GB on the mouse
entrapment recipe); the glyco scorer never reads other candidates. Measured on
a 1,500-protein subset: same rows, peptides and labels, 16 of 7,113 rows differ
in RawScore/CandidateRankEntropy only.

Measured, one session, one binary, one database, Percolator --seed 42 -Y
(4-thread 16 GB VM, both arms with the sequon-only index; arm B reproduces the
README quick tier within seed noise):

                              off        auto
  glycoPSMs @1%              7,109      7,225
  entrapment FDP (1:1)       1.10%      0.91%  (CI 0.62-1.29)
  pGlyco2 confirmed (3,877)  3,361      3,444  (+89 / -6, all 6 FDR-rejected)
  MSFragger confirmed        2,669      2,746
  peptidoform agreement      96.3%      96.8%
  the 84 target spectra          0         69 confirmed (+5 FDR-rejected)
  accepted at +3/+4/+5/+6        -   16/80/50/15; 0 entrapment; HexNAc3 1.2% at +4

Offline (dump, 23 s): the fit reaches 3,783 of 3,824 resolvable reference
scans vs 3,671 without correction, 1 wrong shift. The Thermo reader's precursor
m/z equals both the isolation target and the trailer Monoisotopic M/Z on all
45,905 MS2 (step 1 of #64): the +4 scans are firmware picks.

